From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:01:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] feat(shader): per-stage loop limits with
 APS5_LOOP_GUARD=stages

APS5_LOOP_GUARD gave every stage one limit. A limit loose enough for a
compute program's long loops lets a pixel or vertex program whose loop
bound came from data the host got wrong run for long enough to hang the
GPU first: another translation layer that runs the same kind of title
lost the device early with every single limit from 2^20 down to 1024,
and kept it with 128 iterations in pixel programs, 256 in vertex and
mesh programs and 4096 in compute programs.

APS5_LOOP_GUARD=stages gives those limits (tessellation and local
programs take the vertex one), and APS5_LOOP_GUARD_PIXEL, _VERTEX, _MESH
and _COMPUTE override one stage while APS5_LOOP_GUARD is set. A single
numeric limit behaves, and keys the disk cache, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
