index 882956ed36..975947d127 100644
--- a/docs/dev/ENVIRONMENT.md
+++ b/docs/dev/ENVIRONMENT.md
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ The code reads environment names through `getenv`, `IsEnvironmentSet`, `kibSetti
 
 `APS5_LOOP_GUARD=<iterations>` (decimal or `0x` hex) makes every loop of a recompiled program leave after that many iterations per entry (`core/shader/recompiler/LoopGuard.hpp`, `SpirvBackend/src/SpirvFlowEmitter.cpp`); `0` or an unset variable disables it. Each loop counts its back edges in a variable of its own, cleared when the loop is entered; once the count reaches the limit, its conditional exits leave, every other loop of the invocation leaves at its next conditional exit, and the invocation records one `LoopLimit` fault (address: shader hash, bytes: the limit, instruction: PC of the first exit the guard forced). Loops that finish sooner run as before. Programs with loops then bind a fault buffer, and the disk cache keys on the value. A loop whose exits are all unconditional branches inside its body is not stopped. Its presence separately enables the AGC fault buffer, as listed under `libSceAgcDriver`.
 
+`APS5_LOOP_GUARD=stages` gives each stage its own limit instead: 128 iterations in pixel programs, 256 in vertex, tessellation and mesh programs, and 4096 in compute programs. With `APS5_LOOP_GUARD` set, `APS5_LOOP_GUARD_PIXEL`, `APS5_LOOP_GUARD_VERTEX` (vertex, local and tessellation programs), `APS5_LOOP_GUARD_MESH` and `APS5_LOOP_GUARD_COMPUTE` set one stage's limit (`0` leaves that stage unguarded); without it they do nothing. The disk cache keys on every stage's limit.
+
 | Name | Kind | Source | Default | Description |
 |------|------|--------|---------|-------------|
 | `ANYPS5_NO_SHADER_CACHE` | string | `core/shader/recompiler/ShaderDiskCache.cpp` |  | disables the on-disk shader cache when set to a non-empty value other than 0 |
